# Rule 03. ARIA in composition is static

Language-agnostic. Zones, `{kit}` and "reactive ARIA state" are defined in rule 00.
The syntax per stack is in the runtime appendix.

## Goal

Accessibility behavior does not depend on framework state computed in screens.
Composition markup describes structure and naming. The kit owns how a state
becomes an attribute.

## Rules

1. Native HTML5 semantics first. Add ARIA only where the native element
   cannot express the role.
2. In composition, an `aria-*` attribute is static: a literal value. It is
   never an expression of state, props, effects, watchers or bindings.
3. State reaches ARIA only through a primitive prop: `<Button pressed={on}>`,
   `<Tab selected={i === current}>`. Passing a value to such a prop is allowed;
   the primitive in `{kit}` maps it to `aria-pressed`, `aria-selected` and so on.
   If the primitive has no such prop, add it to the kit (its spec) instead of
   writing the attribute in the screen.
4. Names come from `Label`, a naming prop of the primitive (`AriaLabel`,
   `labelledBy`), or `aria-label` / `aria-labelledby` / `aria-describedby` with a
   value from content or props. Naming attributes are not state and may be
   expressions.
5. Screens never write `data-ui8kit*` contract attributes by hand.
6. Keep the kit focus ring. Dialogs have a name, a description, an Escape
   close and focus return. One `main` per page with `id=main-content`.

## Future (not in force)

A behavior library (`@ui8kit/aria`: `data-ui8kit*` contract attributes, a single
bootstrap that registers the used patterns, a deferred init) is planned. It
does not exist in this repo yet, so its rules are not enforced.

## Validation

`bun run check`, group `rules`, detector `reactive-aria`, fails on a new
`aria-*` attribute with an expression value in a composition file, except the
naming attributes `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, `aria-describedby`,
`aria-haspopup`, `aria-roledescription` (rule 4). The spec-level check is the
`a11y` group (known ARIA names, tables, inputs, sortable headers).
